// Reducer for the head-colon spin class: a ':' HEADING an expression
// parse has no owner (every legal ':' — ternary, case label, range-for,
// label, bitfield — consumes a left side first), and the old pushback
// handed the SAME token back to the caller's loop forever. Statement
// context here (assignment to an existing carrier); the call-argument
// context spins identically. Must ERROR, never hang.
// Oracle: g++ `v = {1: 2};` -> "expected '}' before ':'".
int main()
{
	var m = {};
	m = { "a": 1 };
	return 0;
}
